      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Because MAOIs are potent, even small, consistent amounts of high-tyramine foods like salami can pose a risk of a hypertensive crisis. To truly sleep soundly, you must eliminate or severely limit these aged and cured items entirely while you are on the medication. Focus instead on maximizing your protein intake with fresh, safe sources like poultry, fish, and legumes to keep your energy up without the risk.",
      "source": "target",
